                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Phrasal verbs: separable and inseparable",
                    "explanation": "Un phrasal verb es un verbo + partícula con un significado nuevo: fill in (rellenar), look after (cuidar), put up with (aguantar).\n\nSeparables: el objeto puede ir en medio o detrás (fill in the form / fill the form in). Si el objeto es un pronombre, tiene que ir en medio: pick them up (nunca «pick up them»).\n\nInseparables: el objeto siempre va detrás: we'll look after them, we can put up with the noise.\n\nAlgunos no llevan objeto: check in, set off.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Phrasal verb",
                        "Tipo",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "fill in",
                          "separable",
                          "Fill in the form. / Fill it in."
                        ],
                        [
                          "pick up",
                          "separable",
                          "Pick up the bags. / Pick them up."
                        ],
                        [
                          "drop off",
                          "separable",
                          "Drop off your bags. / Drop them off."
                        ],
                        [
                          "look after",
                          "inseparable",
                          "We'll look after them."
                        ],
                        [
                          "put up with",
                          "inseparable",
                          "We can put up with the noise."
                        ],
                        [
                          "check in / check out",
                          "sin objeto",
                          "We're checking in. / We check out at eleven."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Could you fill in this form, please?",
                      "Can we drop off our bags here tomorrow?",
                      "No problem, we'll look after them.",
                      "Just pick them up before you leave."
                    ]
                  }
                },
