                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Polite complaints and requests",
                    "explanation": "En inglés las quejas suenan más educadas si las suavizamos. Unas cuantas fórmulas:\n\n• Para empezar: I'm sorry to bother you, but…\n• Para dar una mala noticia: I'm afraid… (me temo que…)\n• Para pedir algo: Could you…? / Would you mind + -ing? (¿le importaría…?)\n\nOjo con Would you mind…?: si quieres decir que no te importa, respondes Not at all (= no, en absoluto).\n\nPara agradecer: That's very kind of you.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Función",
                        "Expresión",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Empezar",
                          "I'm sorry to bother you, but…",
                          "I'm sorry to bother you, but there's a problem."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Mala noticia",
                          "I'm afraid…",
                          "I'm afraid the shower doesn't work."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pedir",
                          "Could you…?",
                          "Could you send someone?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pedir (muy educado)",
                          "Would you mind + -ing?",
                          "Would you mind sending someone?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Aceptar",
                          "Not at all. / Of course.",
                          "Not at all."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Disculparse",
                          "I'm so sorry about that.",
                          "I'm so sorry about that."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I'm sorry to bother you, but I'm afraid there's a problem with our room.",
                      "Would you mind sending someone to look at the shower?",
                      "Not at all.",
                      "That's very kind of you."
                    ]
                  }
                },
